{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016mFMPbEcKtHhnRm49D7eVM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Codebase Patterns\n2\t\n3\t- PA.md files live in each CU folder (e.g. aesthetic-services/C04/PA.md)\n4\t- Tests use Path(__file__).parent.parent for PROJECT_ROOT, read .md files directly\n5\t- Keep PA documents under 250 lines with compact markdown tables to avoid diff-guard limits\n6\t- WIM modality reference tables use: Modality | Frequency | Intensity | Duration | KP Ref columns\n7\t- Bilingual format: English term (*Bahasa Malaysia term*) inline\n8\t- validators/ has __init__.py; import as `from validators.module import X`\n9\t- Chinese KT files use 第一部分/第二部分 section headers, not Question/Soalan\n10\t- KT question types detectable by header keywords: \"Multiple Choice\", \"True/False\", \"Matching\", \"Scenario\", \"Calculation\", \"Short Answer\" (+ BM/ZH equivalents)\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t# Ralph Progress Log - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  2:45:02 PM\n15\tStarted autonomous agent loop for PRD completion\n16\t\n17\t\n18\t## Pre-analysis for US-001 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n19\tThis user story is a technical writing task, not a Frappe/Python coding task. The agent's work will be focused on updating content within Markdown files.\n20\t\n21\t**Technical Brief for Agent**\n22\t\n23\t*   **Objective:** Enhance the technical accuracy and depth of High Voltage (HV) safety procedures in BEV Information Sheets.\n24\t*   **Files to Modify:**\n25\t    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-01.md`\n26\t    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-02.md`\n27\t    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-03.md`\n28\t*   **Frappe/Python Involvement:** None. The story does not pertain to Python code, Frappe DocTypes, or hooks. The task is purely content and documentation based.\n29\t*   **Implementation Approach:**\n30\t    1.  **Research Regulations:** Review content to ensure it aligns with Malaysia's OSHA 1994 and EQA 1974, plus specific BEV manufacturer standards.\n31\t    2.  **Verify PPE:** Update Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) details to be precise for BEV Level 3 work, specifically mentioning Class 0 gloves and CAT-III multimeter requirements.\n32\t    3.  **Add Bilingual Terms:** For key technical concepts, ensure both English (EN) and Bahasa Malaysia (BM) terms are present.\n33\t    4.  **Cite Sources:** Add references or footnotes to link claims to the correct regulations.\n34\t*   **Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\n35\t    *   **Diff Size Limit:** The previous attempt failed for creating too large of a diff. Apply changes incrementally and avoid reformatting entire documents to stay under the 500-line change limit.\n36\t    *   **Regulatory Precision:** Ensure citations are to the specific, correct sections of the referenced Malaysian laws.\n37\t    *   **Standards Accuracy:** Double-check that the PPE specifications are current and match industry best practices for HV electrical work.\n38\t\n39\t\n40\t## Story US-001 — Enhance BEV C01 KP technical depth — HV safety procedures and PPE specifications\n41\t\n42\t### What was implemented\n43\t- KP-01: Updated safety glasses spec from DIN EN166 to MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 (Malaysian standard); added Electricity Supply Act 1990 (Act 447) to references with bilingual name\n44\t- KP-02: Added bilingual heading for Digital Multimeter section; added IEC 61010-1 / MS IEC 61010-1 standard reference to DMM spec; added OSHA 1994 (Act 514), EQA 1974 (Act 127), ESA 1990 (Act 447) to References\n45\t- KP-03: Added OSHA 1994 and ESA 1990 citations at start of safety section; added explicit PPE table with Class 0 gloves, CAT-III multimeter, MS ISO 16321 glasses; added BM term for LOTO (Kunci-Keluar/Tag-Keluar); added Malaysian regulatory references\n46\t\n47\t### Patterns discovered\n48\t- diff size anti-pattern: previous attempt generated 2183 lines by rewriting entire files. Correct approach: surgical edits only (66 lines total)\n49\t- KP-01 was already mostly compliant; focused changes were just adding the missing Electricity Supply Act ref and updating safety glasses spec\n50\t- CAT-III multimeter specification is a TOOL spec (not PPE), so only relevant in KP-02 (health check) and KP-03 (maintenance) — not KP-01 (workplace prep)\n51\t\n52\t### Gotchas\n53\t- Windows: must use encoding=utf-8 when opening files with Python\n54\t- Malaysian standard for safety glasses is MS ISO 16321 (not DIN EN166)\n55\t- Act numbers: OSHA = Act 514, EQA = Act 127, ESA = Act 447, Road Transport = Act 333\n56\t\n57\t## Pre-analysis for US-002 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n58\t**Subject: Technical Brief for US-002: Enhance BEV Technical Knowledge Content**\n59\t\n60\t**Note:** The user story provided (US-002) is for enhancing Markdown-based technical documentation, not a Frappe/Python implementation. The following brief is adjusted accordingly.\n61\t\n62\t**1. Target Files:**\n63\tThis task involves modifying Markdown (`.md`) files, not Python code. The specific files are:\n64\t- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-01.md`\n65\t- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-02.md`\n66\t- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-03.md`\n67\t- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-04.md`\n68\t- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-05.md`\n69\t- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-06.md`\n70\t\n71\t**2. Frappe Context:**\n72\tThere are no Frappe DocTypes or hooks involved. The work is confined to editing the content of the specified Markdown files.\n73\t\n74\t**3. Implementation Approach:**\n75\tThe agent should read, analyze, and rewrite the content within each of the six KP files. The goal is to enhance the technical theory for BEV rectification, focusing on:\n76\t- Battery Management System (BMS) components.\n77\t- High-Voltage (HV) cable, On-Board Charger (OBC), and battery pack theory.\n78\t- DC-DC converter function and failure modes.\n79\t- Add clear descriptions for diagrams and include tables for component specifications.\n80\t\n81\t**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n82\t- **CRITICAL:** A previous attempt failed due to an `oversized_diff`. The agent must modify files incrementally. Process one file at a time to keep changes under the 5,000-line diff limit.\n83\t- Ensure High-Voltage safety warnings are made prominent using Markdown callouts (e.g., `> **WARNING:** ...`).\n84\t- Technical accuracy is paramount; content should be precise.\n85\t- The scope is strictly limited to the content of the six listed files.\n86\t\n87\t\n88\t## Story US-002 — Enhance BEV C02 KP — BMS components, HV cable, OBC, battery pack theory\n89\t\n90\t### What was implemented\n91\t- KP-01: Fixed safety glasses spec (DIN EN166 → MS ISO 16321), added BMS component overview table with BM terms and failure modes column, added WARNING callout\n92\t- KP-02: Added prominent WARNING callout for HV cable contact hazard, added HV cable/connector failure modes table\n93\t- KP-03: Added WARNING callout for OBC residual HV risk, added OBC component specifications table (AC input, power ratings, cooling, communication)\n94\t- KP-04: Added WARNING callout for pre-charge component hazards, added pre-charge system failure modes table (relay, resistor, contactor)\n95\t- KP-05: Added WARNING callout with thermal runaway warning, added traction battery pack failure modes table\n96\t- KP-06: Added WARNING callout for DC-DC HV input, converted prose failure symptoms to structured failure modes table\n97\t\n98\t### Patterns discovered\n99\t- previous anti-pattern was oversized_diff (261,809 lines) from complete file rewrites. Correct approach: surgical additions only — 104 lines total for 6 files\n100\t- WARNING callout pattern: `> **AMARAN / WARNING:** [specific hazard relevant to this component]` — each KP gets one targeted warning in the safety section"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171375c8-4f5f-4704-ba14-a7a2cea3ac52","uuid":"8b05f6b0-c25a-4375-856c-b77f7d34db7f","timestamp":"2026-04-17T05:27:47.540Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\progress.txt","content":"## Codebase Patterns\n\n- PA.md files live in each CU folder (e.g. aesthetic-services/C04/PA.md)\n- Tests use Path(__file__).parent.parent for PROJECT_ROOT, read .md files directly\n- Keep PA documents under 250 lines with compact markdown tables to avoid diff-guard limits\n- WIM modality reference tables use: Modality | Frequency | Intensity | Duration | KP Ref columns\n- Bilingual format: English term (*Bahasa Malaysia term*) inline\n- validators/ has __init__.py; import as `from validators.module import X`\n- Chinese KT files use 第一部分/第二部分 section headers, not Question/Soalan\n- KT question types detectable by header keywords: \"Multiple Choice\", \"True/False\", \"Matching\", \"Scenario\", \"Calculation\", \"Short Answer\" (+ BM/ZH equivalents)\n\n---\n\n# Ralph Progress Log - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  2:45:02 PM\nStarted autonomous agent loop for PRD completion\n\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-001 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\nThis user story is a technical writing task, not a Frappe/Python coding task. The agent's work will be focused on updating content within Markdown files.\n\n**Technical Brief for Agent**\n\n*   **Objective:** Enhance the technical accuracy and depth of High Voltage (HV) safety procedures in BEV Information Sheets.\n*   **Files to Modify:**\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-01.md`\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-02.md`\n    *   `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C01/KP-03.md`\n*   **Frappe/Python Involvement:** None. The story does not pertain to Python code, Frappe DocTypes, or hooks. The task is purely content and documentation based.\n*   **Implementation Approach:**\n    1.  **Research Regulations:** Review content to ensure it aligns with Malaysia's OSHA 1994 and EQA 1974, plus specific BEV manufacturer standards.\n    2.  **Verify PPE:** Update Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) details to be precise for BEV Level 3 work, specifically mentioning Class 0 gloves and CAT-III multimeter requirements.\n    3.  **Add Bilingual Terms:** For key technical concepts, ensure both English (EN) and Bahasa Malaysia (BM) terms are present.\n    4.  **Cite Sources:** Add references or footnotes to link claims to the correct regulations.\n*   **Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\n    *   **Diff Size Limit:** The previous attempt failed for creating too large of a diff. Apply changes incrementally and avoid reformatting entire documents to stay under the 500-line change limit.\n    *   **Regulatory Precision:** Ensure citations are to the specific, correct sections of the referenced Malaysian laws.\n    *   **Standards Accuracy:** Double-check that the PPE specifications are current and match industry best practices for HV electrical work.\n\n\n## Story US-001 — Enhance BEV C01 KP technical depth — HV safety procedures and PPE specifications\n\n### What was implemented\n- KP-01: Updated safety glasses spec from DIN EN166 to MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 (Malaysian standard); added Electricity Supply Act 1990 (Act 447) to references with bilingual name\n- KP-02: Added bilingual heading for Digital Multimeter section; added IEC 61010-1 / MS IEC 61010-1 standard reference to DMM spec; added OSHA 1994 (Act 514), EQA 1974 (Act 127), ESA 1990 (Act 447) to References\n- KP-03: Added OSHA 1994 and ESA 1990 citations at start of safety section; added explicit PPE table with Class 0 gloves, CAT-III multimeter, MS ISO 16321 glasses; added BM term for LOTO (Kunci-Keluar/Tag-Keluar); added Malaysian regulatory references\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- diff size anti-pattern: previous attempt generated 2183 lines by rewriting entire files. Correct approach: surgical edits only (66 lines total)\n- KP-01 was already mostly compliant; focused changes were just adding the missing Electricity Supply Act ref and updating safety glasses spec\n- CAT-III multimeter specification is a TOOL spec (not PPE), so only relevant in KP-02 (health check) and KP-03 (maintenance) — not KP-01 (workplace prep)\n\n### Gotchas\n- Windows: must use encoding=utf-8 when opening files with Python\n- Malaysian standard for safety glasses is MS ISO 16321 (not DIN EN166)\n- Act numbers: OSHA = Act 514, EQA = Act 127, ESA = Act 447, Road Transport = Act 333\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-002 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n**Subject: Technical Brief for US-002: Enhance BEV Technical Knowledge Content**\n\n**Note:** The user story provided (US-002) is for enhancing Markdown-based technical documentation, not a Frappe/Python implementation. The following brief is adjusted accordingly.\n\n**1. Target Files:**\nThis task involves modifying Markdown (`.md`) files, not Python code. The specific files are:\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-01.md`\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-02.md`\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-03.md`\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-04.md`\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-05.md`\n- `bev-diagnostic-rectification/C02/KP-06.md`\n\n**2. Frappe Context:**\nThere are no Frappe DocTypes or hooks involved. The work is confined to editing the content of the specified Markdown files.\n\n**3. Implementation Approach:**\nThe agent should read, analyze, and rewrite the content within each of the six KP files. The goal is to enhance the technical theory for BEV rectification, focusing on:\n- Battery Management System (BMS) components.\n- High-Voltage (HV) cable, On-Board Charger (OBC), and battery pack theory.\n- DC-DC converter function and failure modes.\n- Add clear descriptions for diagrams and include tables for component specifications.\n\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n- **CRITICAL:** A previous attempt failed due to an `oversized_diff`. The agent must modify files incrementally. Process one file at a time to keep changes under the 5,000-line diff limit.\n- Ensure High-Voltage safety warnings are made prominent using Markdown callouts (e.g., `> **WARNING:** ...`).\n- Technical accuracy is paramount; content should be precise.\n- The scope is strictly limited to the content of the six listed files.\n\n\n## Story US-002 — Enhance BEV C02 KP — BMS components, HV cable, OBC, battery pack theory\n\n### What was implemented\n- KP-01: Fixed safety glasses spec (DIN EN166 → MS ISO 16321), added BMS component overview table with BM terms and failure modes column, added WARNING callout\n- KP-02: Added prominent WARNING callout for HV cable contact hazard, added HV cable/connector failure modes table\n- KP-03: Added WARNING callout for OBC residual HV risk, added OBC component specifications table (AC input, power ratings, cooling, communication)\n- KP-04: Added WARNING callout for pre-charge component hazards, added pre-charge system failure modes table (relay, resistor, contactor)\n- KP-05: Added WARNING callout with thermal runaway warning, added traction battery pack failure modes table\n- KP-06: Added WARNING callout for DC-DC HV input, converted prose failure symptoms to structured failure modes table\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- previous anti-pattern was oversized_diff (261,809 lines) from complete file rewrites. Correct approach: surgical additions only — 104 lines total for 6 files\n- WARNING callout pattern: `> **AMARAN / WARNING:** [specific hazard relevant to this component]` — each KP gets one targeted warning in the safety section","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1888}}}
