{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0144pjvDDNzUeV7QZsAYyDC1","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t- WARNING callout pattern: `> **AMARAN / WARNING:** [specific hazard relevant to this component]` — each KP gets one targeted warning in the safety section\n101\t- failure modes table pattern: | Component | Failure Mode | Symptom | Diagnosis | — 5-7 rows per file\n102\t- specs table pattern: | Parameter | Specification | — placed after the definition/function section\n103\t\n104\t### Gotchas\n105\t- KP-01 had DIN EN166 (European) instead of MS ISO 16321 (Malaysian standard) for safety glasses — same fix as C01\n106\t- Each KP file already had good base content — surgical additions were sufficient, no rewrites needed\n107\t## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:12:23 PM\n108\tCompleted: Enhance BEV C02 KP — BMS components, HV cable, OBC, battery pack theory (ID: US-002) in 6m\n109\t\n110\t\n111\t## Pre-analysis for US-003 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n112\tThis user story is a content enhancement task, not a Frappe/Python implementation. The following technical brief has been adjusted to reflect the actual task of modifying Markdown documentation.\n113\t\n114\t**Technical Brief: US-003 - BEV Knowledge Point Enhancement**\n115\t\n116\t1.  **Target Files (Content Modification):**\n117\t    *   This is a documentation task; no Python files are involved.\n118\t    *   The work involves editing Markdown (`.md`) files within the `bev-diagnostic-rectification/` directory.\n119\t    *   Files for C03 (Thermal Cooling): `C03/KP-01.md`, `C03/KP-02.md`, `C03/KP-03.md`.\n120\t    *   Files for C04 (Drive Train): `C04/KP-01.md` through `C04/KP-05.md`.\n121\t\n122\t2.  **Frappe/Application Context:**\n123\t    *   No Frappe DocTypes, hooks, or server-side logic are applicable. The task is confined to the content layer of the knowledge base.\n124\t\n125\t3.  **Recommended Implementation Approach:**\n126\t    *   For C03 KPs: Systematically review and enhance content on BEV thermal management. Ensure detailed descriptions of liquid cooling systems, components, and BEV-specific HVAC functions. Add troubleshooting theory.\n127\t    *   For C04 KPs: Review and expand on the electric drive train. Detail the architecture, the role of inverters, theory of traction motors (AC induction vs. permanent magnet), and the principles of regenerative braking and brake control.\n128\t\n129\t4.  **Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n130\t    *   **Primary Constraint:** All added content MUST align with \"manufacturer service manual standards.\" This requires a formal, precise, and technically accurate tone.\n131\t    *   The content should remain theoretical (\"Knowledge Point\") and avoid becoming a step-by-step repair guide.\n132\t    *   Ensure consistency in terminology (e.g., \"transaxle,\" \"inverter\") across all edited documents.\n133\t\n134\t\n135\t## Story US-003 — Enhance BEV C03-C04 KP — thermal cooling and electric drive train theory\n136\t\n137\t### What was implemented\n138\t- C03/KP-01: Added WARNING callout for HV electric pump/compressor hazard; added dielectric coolant (cecair penyejuk dielektrik) awareness section with BM terms\n139\t- C03/KP-02: Added WARNING callout for HV-connected cooling components; added cooling system failure modes table (6 rows: pump, hose, expansion tank, thermostat valve, heat exchanger, temp sensor)\n140\t- C03/KP-03: Added WARNING callout for HV electric compressor; added heat pump system (sistem pam haba) theory section explaining efficiency vs PTC; renumbered subsections 2.3-2.6; added HVAC failure modes table (6 rows)\n141\t- C04/KP-01: Added CU title heading; added WARNING callout covering inverter capacitor discharge hazard; added BM bilingual terms for key drive train components\n142\t- C04/KP-02: Added WARNING callout for capacitor residual charge (10 min wait + 60V verification); added FOC/Vector Control theory section; added inverter specifications table (DC voltage, power, switching freq, efficiency)\n143\t- C04/KP-03: Added WARNING callout for back-EMF hazard on motor phase cables; added regenerative braking theory section (generator mode, limitations table, blending); added motor failure modes table (6 rows)\n144\t- C04/KP-04: Added WARNING callout for heavy HV e-axle assembly; added transaxle failure modes table (5 rows: gears, differential, seals, CV joints, lubricant)\n145\t- C04/KP-05: Added WARNING callout for safety-critical system; added regenerative-friction blending table (6 conditions with contribution split); renumbered section 1.3→1.4\n146\t\n147\t### Patterns discovered\n148\t- Established pattern continues: each KP gets one WARNING callout at the top of the first content section, one failure modes table near the end, and one specifications/theory addition\n149\t- Section renumbering is necessary when inserting new subsections — be careful to check sequential numbering\n150\t- C04 files initially lacked CU heading — add it for consistency with C03 files\n151\t\n152\t### Gotchas\n153\t- C03/KP-03 had subsections 2.2-2.5 that needed renumbering to 2.3-2.6 after inserting heat pump section as 2.2\n154\t- Motor back-EMF warning is unique: even after HV isolation, moving the rotor generates voltage — important safety note not present in inverter KP\n155\t- Regenerative braking limitations are a key theory point for C04: SOC, temperature, speed, ABS activation all disable or limit regeneration\n156\t## Iteration 2 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:21:09 PM\n157\tCompleted: Enhance BEV C03-C04 KP — thermal cooling and electric drive train theory (ID: US-003) in 7m\n158\t\n159\t\n160\t## Pre-analysis for US-005 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n161\t**To:** Claude Code Agent\n162\t**From:** Gemini\n163\t**Subject:** Technical Brief for US-005: Enhance Practical Procedure DocType\n164\t\n165\tThis brief outlines the implementation for a user story on enhancing practical work procedures within the `lhdn_payroll_integration` custom Frappe app.\n166\t\n167\t**1. Python Files & DocTypes to Modify:**\n168\t*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.py`: For server-side validation hooks.\n169\t*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.js`: For client-side UI arrangement/validation.\n170\t*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.json`: The primary DocType definition.\n171\t*   Child DocTypes to create/update: `Procedure Step` and `Assessment Item`.\n172\t\n173\t**2. Frappe DocTypes and Hooks:**\n174\t*   **Primary DocType:** A `Work Sheet` DocType to manage procedures. It should have `Text` or `Table` fields for `ppe_requirements`, `equipment_list`, and `safety_precautions`.\n175\t*   **Child DocTypes:**\n176\t    *   `Procedure Step`: A table containing step-by-step instructions.\n177\t    *   `Assessment Item`: A table with a `Select` field for `domain` (Process, Output, Attitude, Safety, Environment) and a `Text` field for the assessment criteria.\n178\t*   **Hooks (in work_sheet.py):**\n179\t    *   `validate`: To enforce the acceptance criteria.\n180\t\n181\t**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\n182\t1.  Update the `Work Sheet` DocType, ensuring `safety_precautions` is a separate field.\n183\t2.  In `work_sheet.js`, use custom scripting to render the safety field prominently at the top of the form.\n184\t3.  In `work_sheet.py`, implement the `validate` hook to check that the `Assessment Item` child table contains at least one entry for each of the five required domains before saving the document.\n185\t4.  The logic should also verify that the `equipment_list` field is not empty.\n186\t\n187\t**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n188\t*   The story implies updating existing records. A patch script might be necessary to backfill data for the new checklist and equipment list structure in existing `Work Sheet` documents.\n189\t*   The acceptance criterion for \"logical sequence\" is subjective; enforcing a numbered step sequence in the `Procedure Step` table is the most practical approach.\n190\t*   Ensure any new mandatory fields have default values or are handled gracefully by the migration patch to avoid breaking existing records.\n191\t\n192\t## Story US-005 — Enhance BEV KK practical procedures — step-by-step accuracy and safety checklists\n193\t\n194\t### What was implemented\n195\t- C01/KK-01, KK-02, KK-03: Fixed safety glasses spec from DIN EN166 to MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 (Malaysian standard)\n196\t- C02/KK-01: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; expanded placeholder Step 2.1-2.5; restructured checklist to 5-domain structure with Remarks column\n197\t- C02/KK-02: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; added numbered safety precautions list; restructured checklist to 5 domains\n198\t- C02/KK-03: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; fixed AMARAN: format; added numbered safety precautions; restructured checklist to 5 domains\n199\t\n200\t### Patterns discovered\n201\t- C01 KK files were well-structured but had DIN EN166 glasses spec error carried over from KP files\n202\t- C02 KK files used compact inline lists instead of tables at initial creation\n203\t- 5-domain checklist structure (PROCESS/OUTPUT/ATTITUDE/SAFETY/ENVIRONMENT) from C01 is the standard for all KK files\n204\t- Assessment checklist requires Remarks column (5 columns total)\n205\t\n206\t### Gotchas\n207\t- C02/KK-03 used AMARAN: without the / WARNING: bilingual suffix — always use AMARAN / WARNING: format\n208\t- C02/KK-01 Step 2 was a placeholder referencing another file — must always expand placeholders before submission\n209\t- Coolant in OBC work is SW305 scheduled waste — must appear in both safety precautions and ENVIRONMENT domain of checklist\n210\t## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:38:23 PM\n211\tCompleted: Enhance BEV KK practical procedures — step-by-step accuracy and safety checklists (ID: US-005) in 9m\n212\t\n213\t\n214\t## Pre-analysis for US-007 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n215\tHere is the technical brief for user story US-007.\n216\t\n217\t**Subject: Technical Brief for US-007: Enhance Aesthetic KPs**\n218\t\n219\tThis story is a content enhancement task, not a Python coding task. The agent will review and update existing Markdown knowledge package (KP) files.\n220\t\n221\t**1. Target Files (Markdown, not Python):**\n222\t- `aesthetic-services/C01/KP-01.md` through `KP-05.md`\n223\t- `aesthetic-services/C02/KP-01.md` through `KP-07.md`\n224\t\n225\t**2. Frappe DocTypes/Hooks:**\n226\t- No direct interaction with DocTypes or hooks is expected. The task is confined to updating the content of the specified `.md` files.\n227\t\n228\t**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\n229\t- Read each target `.md` file.\n230\t- Review content against acceptance criteria:\n231\t    - C01: Correctness of consultation techniques, BMI calculation, body typing.\n232\t    - C02: Accuracy of thermal therapy details, safety, and contraindications.\n233\t- Enhance the text for anatomical and physiological accuracy.\n234\t- Ensure all key concepts include required bilingual (English/local language) terminology.\n235\t- Overwrite the existing files with the updated, reviewed content.\n236\t\n237\t**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n238\t- **Bilingual Accuracy:** This is a critical requirement. The agent must provide correct translations for technical terms.\n239\t- **Subject-Matter Expertise:** The content is technical. The agent must ensure the information on anatomy, BMI, and thermal therapies is accurate and up-to-date.\n240\t\n241\t\n242\t## Story US-007 — Enhance Aesthetic C01-C02 KP — body consultation and thermal therapy theory\n243\t\n244\t### What was implemented\n245\t- C01/KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for disinfectant chemical hazards; enhanced magnifying lamp usage detail; added flexible measuring tape to tools table\n246\t- C01/KP-03: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout before contraindications section; added calliper skinfold measurement sites table (4 sites with location + client position); added Waist-Hip Ratio (WHR) section with formula and risk classification table; renumbered 9.3 → 9.4 for Limitations\n247\t- C02/KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout before contraindications section; added thermal therapy modalities overview table with bilingual terms (6 modalities including body wrap)\n248\t- C02/KP-02: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for electrical safety in thermal equipment room\n249\t- C02/KP-05: Added body wrap (balutan badan) as modality 2.6 with full parameter table, procedure overview, and product types table; restructured section 4.0 with per-modality contraindications table and general precautions subsections"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171375c8-4f5f-4704-ba14-a7a2cea3ac52","uuid":"a496ca6c-96d7-4497-865d-53bbd58b1097","timestamp":"2026-04-17T05:27:50.133Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\progress.txt","content":"- WARNING callout pattern: `> **AMARAN / WARNING:** [specific hazard relevant to this component]` — each KP gets one targeted warning in the safety section\n- failure modes table pattern: | Component | Failure Mode | Symptom | Diagnosis | — 5-7 rows per file\n- specs table pattern: | Parameter | Specification | — placed after the definition/function section\n\n### Gotchas\n- KP-01 had DIN EN166 (European) instead of MS ISO 16321 (Malaysian standard) for safety glasses — same fix as C01\n- Each KP file already had good base content — surgical additions were sufficient, no rewrites needed\n## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:12:23 PM\nCompleted: Enhance BEV C02 KP — BMS components, HV cable, OBC, battery pack theory (ID: US-002) in 6m\n\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-003 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\nThis user story is a content enhancement task, not a Frappe/Python implementation. The following technical brief has been adjusted to reflect the actual task of modifying Markdown documentation.\n\n**Technical Brief: US-003 - BEV Knowledge Point Enhancement**\n\n1.  **Target Files (Content Modification):**\n    *   This is a documentation task; no Python files are involved.\n    *   The work involves editing Markdown (`.md`) files within the `bev-diagnostic-rectification/` directory.\n    *   Files for C03 (Thermal Cooling): `C03/KP-01.md`, `C03/KP-02.md`, `C03/KP-03.md`.\n    *   Files for C04 (Drive Train): `C04/KP-01.md` through `C04/KP-05.md`.\n\n2.  **Frappe/Application Context:**\n    *   No Frappe DocTypes, hooks, or server-side logic are applicable. The task is confined to the content layer of the knowledge base.\n\n3.  **Recommended Implementation Approach:**\n    *   For C03 KPs: Systematically review and enhance content on BEV thermal management. Ensure detailed descriptions of liquid cooling systems, components, and BEV-specific HVAC functions. Add troubleshooting theory.\n    *   For C04 KPs: Review and expand on the electric drive train. Detail the architecture, the role of inverters, theory of traction motors (AC induction vs. permanent magnet), and the principles of regenerative braking and brake control.\n\n4.  **Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n    *   **Primary Constraint:** All added content MUST align with \"manufacturer service manual standards.\" This requires a formal, precise, and technically accurate tone.\n    *   The content should remain theoretical (\"Knowledge Point\") and avoid becoming a step-by-step repair guide.\n    *   Ensure consistency in terminology (e.g., \"transaxle,\" \"inverter\") across all edited documents.\n\n\n## Story US-003 — Enhance BEV C03-C04 KP — thermal cooling and electric drive train theory\n\n### What was implemented\n- C03/KP-01: Added WARNING callout for HV electric pump/compressor hazard; added dielectric coolant (cecair penyejuk dielektrik) awareness section with BM terms\n- C03/KP-02: Added WARNING callout for HV-connected cooling components; added cooling system failure modes table (6 rows: pump, hose, expansion tank, thermostat valve, heat exchanger, temp sensor)\n- C03/KP-03: Added WARNING callout for HV electric compressor; added heat pump system (sistem pam haba) theory section explaining efficiency vs PTC; renumbered subsections 2.3-2.6; added HVAC failure modes table (6 rows)\n- C04/KP-01: Added CU title heading; added WARNING callout covering inverter capacitor discharge hazard; added BM bilingual terms for key drive train components\n- C04/KP-02: Added WARNING callout for capacitor residual charge (10 min wait + 60V verification); added FOC/Vector Control theory section; added inverter specifications table (DC voltage, power, switching freq, efficiency)\n- C04/KP-03: Added WARNING callout for back-EMF hazard on motor phase cables; added regenerative braking theory section (generator mode, limitations table, blending); added motor failure modes table (6 rows)\n- C04/KP-04: Added WARNING callout for heavy HV e-axle assembly; added transaxle failure modes table (5 rows: gears, differential, seals, CV joints, lubricant)\n- C04/KP-05: Added WARNING callout for safety-critical system; added regenerative-friction blending table (6 conditions with contribution split); renumbered section 1.3→1.4\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- Established pattern continues: each KP gets one WARNING callout at the top of the first content section, one failure modes table near the end, and one specifications/theory addition\n- Section renumbering is necessary when inserting new subsections — be careful to check sequential numbering\n- C04 files initially lacked CU heading — add it for consistency with C03 files\n\n### Gotchas\n- C03/KP-03 had subsections 2.2-2.5 that needed renumbering to 2.3-2.6 after inserting heat pump section as 2.2\n- Motor back-EMF warning is unique: even after HV isolation, moving the rotor generates voltage — important safety note not present in inverter KP\n- Regenerative braking limitations are a key theory point for C04: SOC, temperature, speed, ABS activation all disable or limit regeneration\n## Iteration 2 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:21:09 PM\nCompleted: Enhance BEV C03-C04 KP — thermal cooling and electric drive train theory (ID: US-003) in 7m\n\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-005 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n**To:** Claude Code Agent\n**From:** Gemini\n**Subject:** Technical Brief for US-005: Enhance Practical Procedure DocType\n\nThis brief outlines the implementation for a user story on enhancing practical work procedures within the `lhdn_payroll_integration` custom Frappe app.\n\n**1. Python Files & DocTypes to Modify:**\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.py`: For server-side validation hooks.\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.js`: For client-side UI arrangement/validation.\n*   `lhdn_payroll_integration/doctype/work_sheet/work_sheet.json`: The primary DocType definition.\n*   Child DocTypes to create/update: `Procedure Step` and `Assessment Item`.\n\n**2. Frappe DocTypes and Hooks:**\n*   **Primary DocType:** A `Work Sheet` DocType to manage procedures. It should have `Text` or `Table` fields for `ppe_requirements`, `equipment_list`, and `safety_precautions`.\n*   **Child DocTypes:**\n    *   `Procedure Step`: A table containing step-by-step instructions.\n    *   `Assessment Item`: A table with a `Select` field for `domain` (Process, Output, Attitude, Safety, Environment) and a `Text` field for the assessment criteria.\n*   **Hooks (in work_sheet.py):**\n    *   `validate`: To enforce the acceptance criteria.\n\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\n1.  Update the `Work Sheet` DocType, ensuring `safety_precautions` is a separate field.\n2.  In `work_sheet.js`, use custom scripting to render the safety field prominently at the top of the form.\n3.  In `work_sheet.py`, implement the `validate` hook to check that the `Assessment Item` child table contains at least one entry for each of the five required domains before saving the document.\n4.  The logic should also verify that the `equipment_list` field is not empty.\n\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n*   The story implies updating existing records. A patch script might be necessary to backfill data for the new checklist and equipment list structure in existing `Work Sheet` documents.\n*   The acceptance criterion for \"logical sequence\" is subjective; enforcing a numbered step sequence in the `Procedure Step` table is the most practical approach.\n*   Ensure any new mandatory fields have default values or are handled gracefully by the migration patch to avoid breaking existing records.\n\n## Story US-005 — Enhance BEV KK practical procedures — step-by-step accuracy and safety checklists\n\n### What was implemented\n- C01/KK-01, KK-02, KK-03: Fixed safety glasses spec from DIN EN166 to MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 (Malaysian standard)\n- C02/KK-01: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; expanded placeholder Step 2.1-2.5; restructured checklist to 5-domain structure with Remarks column\n- C02/KK-02: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; added numbered safety precautions list; restructured checklist to 5 domains\n- C02/KK-03: Expanded inline equipment text to tables; fixed AMARAN: format; added numbered safety precautions; restructured checklist to 5 domains\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- C01 KK files were well-structured but had DIN EN166 glasses spec error carried over from KP files\n- C02 KK files used compact inline lists instead of tables at initial creation\n- 5-domain checklist structure (PROCESS/OUTPUT/ATTITUDE/SAFETY/ENVIRONMENT) from C01 is the standard for all KK files\n- Assessment checklist requires Remarks column (5 columns total)\n\n### Gotchas\n- C02/KK-03 used AMARAN: without the / WARNING: bilingual suffix — always use AMARAN / WARNING: format\n- C02/KK-01 Step 2 was a placeholder referencing another file — must always expand placeholders before submission\n- Coolant in OBC work is SW305 scheduled waste — must appear in both safety precautions and ENVIRONMENT domain of checklist\n## Iteration 1 - Thu, Apr 16, 2026  9:38:23 PM\nCompleted: Enhance BEV KK practical procedures — step-by-step accuracy and safety checklists (ID: US-005) in 9m\n\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-007 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\nHere is the technical brief for user story US-007.\n\n**Subject: Technical Brief for US-007: Enhance Aesthetic KPs**\n\nThis story is a content enhancement task, not a Python coding task. The agent will review and update existing Markdown knowledge package (KP) files.\n\n**1. Target Files (Markdown, not Python):**\n- `aesthetic-services/C01/KP-01.md` through `KP-05.md`\n- `aesthetic-services/C02/KP-01.md` through `KP-07.md`\n\n**2. Frappe DocTypes/Hooks:**\n- No direct interaction with DocTypes or hooks is expected. The task is confined to updating the content of the specified `.md` files.\n\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\n- Read each target `.md` file.\n- Review content against acceptance criteria:\n    - C01: Correctness of consultation techniques, BMI calculation, body typing.\n    - C02: Accuracy of thermal therapy details, safety, and contraindications.\n- Enhance the text for anatomical and physiological accuracy.\n- Ensure all key concepts include required bilingual (English/local language) terminology.\n- Overwrite the existing files with the updated, reviewed content.\n\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n- **Bilingual Accuracy:** This is a critical requirement. The agent must provide correct translations for technical terms.\n- **Subject-Matter Expertise:** The content is technical. The agent must ensure the information on anatomy, BMI, and thermal therapies is accurate and up-to-date.\n\n\n## Story US-007 — Enhance Aesthetic C01-C02 KP — body consultation and thermal therapy theory\n\n### What was implemented\n- C01/KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for disinfectant chemical hazards; enhanced magnifying lamp usage detail; added flexible measuring tape to tools table\n- C01/KP-03: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout before contraindications section; added calliper skinfold measurement sites table (4 sites with location + client position); added Waist-Hip Ratio (WHR) section with formula and risk classification table; renumbered 9.3 → 9.4 for Limitations\n- C02/KP-01: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout before contraindications section; added thermal therapy modalities overview table with bilingual terms (6 modalities including body wrap)\n- C02/KP-02: Added AMARAN/WARNING callout for electrical safety in thermal equipment room\n- C02/KP-05: Added body wrap (balutan badan) as modality 2.6 with full parameter table, procedure overview, and product types table; restructured section 4.0 with per-modality contraindications table and general precautions subsections","numLines":150,"startLine":100,"totalLines":1888}}}
