{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRpH68W51SGhW9UCVQE9NT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 资料单 1：小儿生理特点与小儿经络（与成人差异）\n2\t\n3\t**WIM 编码：** MP-031-3:2016-E01/KP(1/3)\n4\t**NOSS：** MP-031-3:2016 推拿疗法服务 (Level 3)\n5\t**CU：** E01 小儿推拿服务\n6\t**纸张颜色：** ⚪ 白\n7\t**时数：** 28 小时\n8\t**最后更新：** 2026-04-17\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## 一、学习目标\n12\t\n13\t阅读完本资料单后，学员应能够：\n14\t1. 描述 0–6 岁婴幼儿的生理与解剖特点；\n15\t2. 说明小儿经络发育的特殊性；\n16\t3. 比较小儿与成人在推拿评估中的差异；\n17\t4. 识别小儿推拿前必须完成的安全核查项目。\n18\t\n19\t## 二、小儿推拿概述 / Introduction to Paediatric Tuina\n20\t\n21\t小儿推拿（Paediatric Tuina / 小儿推拿 Xiǎo'ér Tuīná）是中医推拿（Tuina）的专门分支，专门用于 **0–6 岁婴幼儿**。其历史可上溯至明代——《小儿推拿广意》（熊应雄著）系统总结小儿专属手法与穴位；清代《幼科铁镜》（夏鼎著）进一步完善小儿病诊疗体系。NOSS 第 5 页明确指出：在唐代（公元 618–907 年）小儿推拿已具雏形，至明代（1368–1644 年）发展为独立学派。\n22\t\n23\t小儿推拿的核心目标是**调节气（Qi）的循环**，达到改善：\n24\t- 消化（Digestion）— 食欲、排便\n25\t- 呼吸（Respiration）— 缓解感冒、咳嗽\n26\t- 神志（Spirit）— 改善睡眠、缓解夜啼\n27\t- 整体生长发育（Growth & Development）\n28\t\n29\t> **重要边界：** 小儿推拿是**辅助调理**而非替代医疗。任何急症、感染性疾病、外伤皆须由医院诊治。\n30\t\n31\t## 三、小儿生理特点 / Paediatric Physiology\n32\t\n33\t中医经典《小儿药证直诀》（钱乙）总结小儿\"三大生理特点\"：\n34\t\n35\t| 特点 | 中文 | 含义 | 推拿意义 |\n36\t|------|------|------|----------|\n37\t| Tender organs | 脏腑娇嫩 | 五脏六腑功能尚未健全 | 力度必须**轻柔**，避免直接深推 |\n38\t| Qi & form not full | 形气未充 | 气血、肌肉、骨骼仍在发育 | 时间宜**短**（5–30 分钟）|\n39\t| Vigorous vitality | 生机蓬勃 | 复原力强，反应迅速 | 见效快，方案需及时调整 |\n40\t\n41\t### 3.1 解剖差异\n42\t\n43\t| 项目 | 婴幼儿（0–6 岁） | 成人 |\n44\t|------|-----------------|------|\n45\t| 皮肤 | 薄、嫩、含水量高 | 较厚 |\n46\t| 骨骼 | 软骨多、骨化未完成 | 完全骨化 |\n47\t| 头颅 | 1 岁前前囟门未闭 | 完全闭合 |\n48\t| 肌肉 | 体积小、力量弱 | 充实 |\n49\t| 内脏 | 相对位置较高、肝大 | 标准定位 |\n50\t| 体温调节 | 不稳定 | 稳定 |\n51\t| 免疫力 | 低（易感染） | 较高 |\n52\t\n53\t### 3.2 力度与时间参考表\n54\t\n55\t| 年龄 | 力度（指压） | 单次时长 | 注意 |\n56\t|------|------------:|---------:|------|\n57\t| 0–3 月 | 极轻（如抚触） | 5–10 分钟 | 必须有家长抱姿 |\n58\t| 3–12 月 | 轻 | 10–15 分钟 | 注意囟门、避开 |\n59\t| 1–3 岁 | 较轻 | 15–20 分钟 | 玩具配合安抚 |\n60\t| 3–6 岁 | 中等偏轻 | 20–30 分钟 | 可仰卧/俯卧 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171375c8-4f5f-4704-ba14-a7a2cea3ac52","uuid":"c61d0fdb-4865-4355-bf87-5dfb6083f727","timestamp":"2026-04-17T05:31:19.862Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\tuinalogy-services\\E01\\KP-01.md","content":"# 资料单 1：小儿生理特点与小儿经络（与成人差异）\n\n**WIM 编码：** MP-031-3:2016-E01/KP(1/3)\n**NOSS：** MP-031-3:2016 推拿疗法服务 (Level 3)\n**CU：** E01 小儿推拿服务\n**纸张颜色：** ⚪ 白\n**时数：** 28 小时\n**最后更新：** 2026-04-17\n---\n\n## 一、学习目标\n\n阅读完本资料单后，学员应能够：\n1. 描述 0–6 岁婴幼儿的生理与解剖特点；\n2. 说明小儿经络发育的特殊性；\n3. 比较小儿与成人在推拿评估中的差异；\n4. 识别小儿推拿前必须完成的安全核查项目。\n\n## 二、小儿推拿概述 / Introduction to Paediatric Tuina\n\n小儿推拿（Paediatric Tuina / 小儿推拿 Xiǎo'ér Tuīná）是中医推拿（Tuina）的专门分支，专门用于 **0–6 岁婴幼儿**。其历史可上溯至明代——《小儿推拿广意》（熊应雄著）系统总结小儿专属手法与穴位；清代《幼科铁镜》（夏鼎著）进一步完善小儿病诊疗体系。NOSS 第 5 页明确指出：在唐代（公元 618–907 年）小儿推拿已具雏形，至明代（1368–1644 年）发展为独立学派。\n\n小儿推拿的核心目标是**调节气（Qi）的循环**，达到改善：\n- 消化（Digestion）— 食欲、排便\n- 呼吸（Respiration）— 缓解感冒、咳嗽\n- 神志（Spirit）— 改善睡眠、缓解夜啼\n- 整体生长发育（Growth & Development）\n\n> **重要边界：** 小儿推拿是**辅助调理**而非替代医疗。任何急症、感染性疾病、外伤皆须由医院诊治。\n\n## 三、小儿生理特点 / Paediatric Physiology\n\n中医经典《小儿药证直诀》（钱乙）总结小儿\"三大生理特点\"：\n\n| 特点 | 中文 | 含义 | 推拿意义 |\n|------|------|------|----------|\n| Tender organs | 脏腑娇嫩 | 五脏六腑功能尚未健全 | 力度必须**轻柔**，避免直接深推 |\n| Qi & form not full | 形气未充 | 气血、肌肉、骨骼仍在发育 | 时间宜**短**（5–30 分钟）|\n| Vigorous vitality | 生机蓬勃 | 复原力强，反应迅速 | 见效快，方案需及时调整 |\n\n### 3.1 解剖差异\n\n| 项目 | 婴幼儿（0–6 岁） | 成人 |\n|------|-----------------|------|\n| 皮肤 | 薄、嫩、含水量高 | 较厚 |\n| 骨骼 | 软骨多、骨化未完成 | 完全骨化 |\n| 头颅 | 1 岁前前囟门未闭 | 完全闭合 |\n| 肌肉 | 体积小、力量弱 | 充实 |\n| 内脏 | 相对位置较高、肝大 | 标准定位 |\n| 体温调节 | 不稳定 | 稳定 |\n| 免疫力 | 低（易感染） | 较高 |\n\n### 3.2 力度与时间参考表\n\n| 年龄 | 力度（指压） | 单次时长 | 注意 |\n|------|------------:|---------:|------|\n| 0–3 月 | 极轻（如抚触） | 5–10 分钟 | 必须有家长抱姿 |\n| 3–12 月 | 轻 | 10–15 分钟 | 注意囟门、避开 |\n| 1–3 岁 | 较轻 | 15–20 分钟 | 玩具配合安抚 |\n| 3–6 岁 | 中等偏轻 | 20–30 分钟 | 可仰卧/俯卧 |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":182}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01PkdYYLRFEz1Pg1qcet6i2K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012VVqMNSmN5b67Kym54iDLX","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\tuinalogy-services\\E02\\KP-01.md","limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1625,"cache_read_input_tokens":66886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1625},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171375c8-4f5f-4704-ba14-a7a2cea3ac52","uuid":"ec39d28a-3739-4264-b4d9-66ffe96866d7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012VVqMNSmN5b67Kym54iDLX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 资料单 1：妇女生理与推拿适应症 / Women's Physiology & Tuina Indications\n2\t\n3\t**WIM 编码：** MP-031-3:2016-E02/KP(1/3)\n4\t**NOSS：** MP-031-3:2016 推拿疗法服务 (Level 3)\n5\t**CU：** E02 妇女推拿服务 (Woman Tuina Service)\n6\t**纸张颜色：** 白\n7\t**时数：** 26 小时\n8\t**最后更新：** 2026-04-17\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## 学习成果\n12\t\n13\t完成本资料单后，学员能够：\n14\t- 阐述妇女四大生理周期（经、孕、产、更）的中医病机与西医生理基础\n15\t- 说明任脉、冲脉、带脉与女性气血关系\n16\t- 列出妇女推拿的常见适应症与基本调理思路\n17\t- 识别妇女推拿前必须排查的禁忌与转诊征兆\n18\t- 掌握妇女四诊（望、闻、问、切）的重点与隐私沟通要领\n19\t\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t> ⚠️ **Pregnancy Contraindication** — LI-4 (合谷/Hegu), SP-6 (三阴交/Sanyinjiao), GB-21 (肩井/Jianjing) mentioned in this document are forbidden during pregnancy at all trimesters per T&CM Act 2013 Section 28. Do NOT apply to pregnant clients. See `_reference/pregnancy-safety-reference.md`.\n23\t\n24\t\n25\t## 一、妇女生理总论 / Overview of Women's Physiology\n26\t\n27\t中医认为女性\"以血为本，以肝为先天\"，与男性有所不同。女性一生经历**经 (jīng / menstruation)**、**带 (dài / leucorrhoea)**、**胎 (tāi / pregnancy)**、**产 (chǎn / parturition)**、**乳 (rǔ / lactation)** 五大生理活动，皆与冲、任、督、带四脉密切相关。\n28\t\n29\t| 中医观点 | 西医对应 |\n30\t|----------|----------|\n31\t| 肾藏精，主生殖 | 下丘脑—垂体—卵巢轴 (HPO axis) |\n32\t| 肝藏血，主疏泄 | 雌激素与情志调节 |\n33\t| 脾统血 | 凝血与代谢 |\n34\t| 心主血脉 | 心血管系统 |\n35\t| 冲为血海，任主胞胎 | 子宫、卵巢、输卵管 |\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## 二、女性三大经脉 / Three Key Vessels\n40\t\n41\t| 经脉 | 中文 | English | 功能 | 常用穴 |\n42\t|------|------|---------|------|--------|\n43\t| 任脉 | 任脉 | Conception Vessel (Ren) | 总任阴经；主胞胎 | 关元、气海、中极、膻中 |\n44\t| 冲脉 | 冲脉 | Penetrating Vessel (Chong) | 十二经之海；血海 | 横骨、大赫、气穴、公孙（八脉交会） |\n45\t| 带脉 | 带脉 | Belt Vessel (Dai) | 约束诸经；主带下 | 带脉穴、五枢、维道 |\n46\t\n47\t**临床要点：** 任脉穴位（脐下）孕期严禁深按；冲脉、带脉调理多用于经带不调与子宫脱垂。\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## 三、妇女四大生理阶段 / Four Major Stages\n52\t\n53\t### 1. 经期 (Menstruation Phase)\n54\t\n55\t| 项目 | 说明 |\n56\t|------|------|\n57\t| 西医 | 月经周期 21–35 天；行经期 3–7 天；经量 30–80ml |\n58\t| 中医 | 行经为肾气推动，冲任溢满下泄；肝郁则痛、脾虚则量多 |\n59\t| 推拿适应 | 经前/经期痛经、经前胀乳、情志不畅、腰酸 |\n60\t| 推拿禁区 | 腰骶强按；腹部深按；活血强刺激穴 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171375c8-4f5f-4704-ba14-a7a2cea3ac52","uuid":"3e64bd09-5b55-4e24-9ce1-2000f24150f9","timestamp":"2026-04-17T05:31:22.867Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\tuinalogy-services\\E02\\KP-01.md","content":"# 资料单 1：妇女生理与推拿适应症 / Women's Physiology & Tuina Indications\n\n**WIM 编码：** MP-031-3:2016-E02/KP(1/3)\n**NOSS：** MP-031-3:2016 推拿疗法服务 (Level 3)\n**CU：** E02 妇女推拿服务 (Woman Tuina Service)\n**纸张颜色：** 白\n**时数：** 26 小时\n**最后更新：** 2026-04-17\n---\n\n## 学习成果\n\n完成本资料单后，学员能够：\n- 阐述妇女四大生理周期（经、孕、产、更）的中医病机与西医生理基础\n- 说明任脉、冲脉、带脉与女性气血关系\n- 列出妇女推拿的常见适应症与基本调理思路\n- 识别妇女推拿前必须排查的禁忌与转诊征兆\n- 掌握妇女四诊（望、闻、问、切）的重点与隐私沟通要领\n\n---\n\n> ⚠️ **Pregnancy Contraindication** — LI-4 (合谷/Hegu), SP-6 (三阴交/Sanyinjiao), GB-21 (肩井/Jianjing) mentioned in this document are forbidden during pregnancy at all trimesters per T&CM Act 2013 Section 28. Do NOT apply to pregnant clients. See `_reference/pregnancy-safety-reference.md`.\n\n\n## 一、妇女生理总论 / Overview of Women's Physiology\n\n中医认为女性\"以血为本，以肝为先天\"，与男性有所不同。女性一生经历**经 (jīng / menstruation)**、**带 (dài / leucorrhoea)**、**胎 (tāi / pregnancy)**、**产 (chǎn / parturition)**、**乳 (rǔ / lactation)** 五大生理活动，皆与冲、任、督、带四脉密切相关。\n\n| 中医观点 | 西医对应 |\n|----------|----------|\n| 肾藏精，主生殖 | 下丘脑—垂体—卵巢轴 (HPO axis) |\n| 肝藏血，主疏泄 | 雌激素与情志调节 |\n| 脾统血 | 凝血与代谢 |\n| 心主血脉 | 心血管系统 |\n| 冲为血海，任主胞胎 | 子宫、卵巢、输卵管 |\n\n---\n\n## 二、女性三大经脉 / Three Key Vessels\n\n| 经脉 | 中文 | English | 功能 | 常用穴 |\n|------|------|---------|------|--------|\n| 任脉 | 任脉 | Conception Vessel (Ren) | 总任阴经；主胞胎 | 关元、气海、中极、膻中 |\n| 冲脉 | 冲脉 | Penetrating Vessel (Chong) | 十二经之海；血海 | 横骨、大赫、气穴、公孙（八脉交会） |\n| 带脉 | 带脉 | Belt Vessel (Dai) | 约束诸经；主带下 | 带脉穴、五枢、维道 |\n\n**临床要点：** 任脉穴位（脐下）孕期严禁深按；冲脉、带脉调理多用于经带不调与子宫脱垂。\n\n---\n\n## 三、妇女四大生理阶段 / Four Major Stages\n\n### 1. 经期 (Menstruation Phase)\n\n| 项目 | 说明 |\n|------|------|\n| 西医 | 月经周期 21–35 天；行经期 3–7 天；经量 30–80ml |\n| 中医 | 行经为肾气推动，冲任溢满下泄；肝郁则痛、脾虚则量多 |\n| 推拿适应 | 经前/经期痛经、经前胀乳、情志不畅、腰酸 |\n| 推拿禁区 | 腰骶强按；腹部深按；活血强刺激穴 |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":188}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01KhSCgzTDveudruRwSAb7oV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good overview of the TCM terms used in the documents. Let me now create the terminology index and the validator script.\n\nFor the terminology index, I'll compile all the terms from the documents I've read. Let me organize them into 6 categories:\n\n1. **Meridians (经络)** - ~20 terms\n2. **Diagnostics (四诊/八纲)** - ~15 terms\n3. **Five Elements (五行)** - ~10 terms\n4. **Acupoints (穴位)** - ~25 terms\n5. **Techniques (推拿手法)** - ~15 terms\n\n\n6. **Safety (安全)** - ~10 terms\n\nI'll use CU codes for NOSS references where applicable and mark frequency based on document occurrence. Now I need to build out the index file carefully, making sure I capture the exact Chinese characters from the source documents, including the additional vessel terms like 冲脉 and 带脉 that appear in the E02 and E01 documents.\n\nI'm working through the complete meridian system—the eight extraordinary vessels plus all twelve primary meridians across the arm and leg channels, each with their proper Chinese names and English translations. Now I'm moving through the pathological patterns and diagnostic frameworks—looking at how qi and blood imbalances manifest, the various syndromes like cold pathogens and damp-heat, organ system deficiencies, and pulse diagnosis as a key assessment tool. I'm also beginning to organize the Five Elements framework.\n\nContinuing with the Five Elements and their corresponding organ systems—Earth, Metal, and Water complete the cycle, and I'm noting how each organ governs specific tissues and functions: the Liver controls sinews, Kidneys govern bones, the Spleen manages muscles, and the Heart regulates blood vessels. Then I'm moving into the practical application with key acupoints used in treatment, including ST-36, LI-4, SP-6, and several others along the Governing Vessel and other meridians. I'm continuing through the acupuncture points, adding the back meridian points and then cross-referencing with the E02 document to verify the Ren, Chong, and Belt meridian points. Now I'm also noting the key techniques like pushing, kneading, and pressing methods. I'm cross-referencing the eight major techniques against the source documents to establish the canonical list: 推、拿、按、捏、揉、捻、摩、拍. I also notice the pre-competition and post-competition routines use specific combinations of these techniques, and I need to organize the safety considerations—contraindications, indications, precautions, referrals, informed consent, and professional ethics—into a structured reference with proper documentation sources.\n\nNow I'm setting up the terminology index with source references from each curriculum unit, tracking frequency across documents to distinguish between high-frequency terms appearing in five or more units versus medium and low-frequency ones. I'll need to build a validator that checks the index against the actual markdown files to ensure zero deviations from the canonical Chinese characters as they appear in the source materials.\n\nDesigning the validator algorithm... I need to reconsider how to handle punctuation like hyphens within terms. If I'm only extracting consecutive Chinese characters, a term like \"足三-里\" would split into separate sequences \"足三\" and \"里\", which wouldn't match the canonical \"足三里\" even with Levenshtein distance 1. I should probably extract sequences while allowing internal punctuation to stay attached, so \"足三-里\" remains as a single unit for comparison. I'm settling on a more practical approach: generate all single-edit variants of each canonical term (deletions and substitutions at each position), then search the document for these variants and flag any matches as deviations. I should also handle hyphenated forms to catch common formatting variations. Writing the validator implementation... I'm realizing the brute-force approach of checking every position against every canonical term will create too many false positives—like matching \"推拿\" as a near-miss of \"推法\" when they're just different words. Instead, I should tokenize the content first to extract only the Chinese character sequences, then check those tokens against the canonical terms for actual deviations.\n\nBut even that gets tricky with substring matching—if I'm looking for \"气血\" within \"气滞血瘀\", the edit distance calculation becomes ambiguous. I think the real solution is simpler: since I'm building the index from the exact 35 documents being validated, the validator should find zero deviations if everything's consistent. The tool's purpose is to catch actual typos or character variants that slip in, not to be overly aggressive about what counts as a deviation.\n\nLooking at the example again—\"足三里 vs 足三-里\" being flagged—it seems like the rule is just: if a term differs from the canonical form by more than one character edit, flag it. So edit distance > 1 gets flagged, but single-character variations are acceptable.\n\nFor the implementation, I'll set up a validator that catches near-misses within edit distance 1 of canonical terms (allowing for one substitution, insertion, or deletion), while filtering for Chinese sequences of at least 3 characters to minimize false positives.\n\nWriting the validator code... I'm structuring the terminology index with NOSS Reference codes mapping to specific curriculum units (Consultation, Full Body Tuina, Sports Tuina, etc.) and assigning frequency levels based on how many units use each term. Now I need to write out the actual files and make sure the validator script runs correctly from the project root.\n\nThe test expects the validator to create a `term-deviations.txt` file at the project root, and it should be empty if there are no deviations found—that's what the test is checking for.\n\nNow I'm verifying the terminology index against the actual documents to ensure I'm using the exact same Chinese characters. I'm going through the acupoint terms from the documents—checking meridians like 督脉 and 足太阳膀胱经, head points like 百会 and 风池, upper limb points like 肩井 and 合谷, and lower limb points like 足三里 and 三阴交.\n\nI'm also pulling acupoint categories from the shoulder and neck sections—points like 肩井、肩髃、曲池 for the shoulder area and 风池、天柱、大椎 for the neck. With the terminology verified, I'm ready to structure the index into six main categories covering meridians, diagnostics, five elements and organs, and acupoints—roughly 80 terms total organized by system.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1488,"cache_read_input_tokens":68511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1488},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171375c8-4f5f-4704-ba14-a7a2cea3ac52","uuid":"d938e090-479a-45ee-8af5-2bb220c1335b"}
